      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Initial contacts were very good and positive and the installation by and large was well done.  However, I had an immediate problem with the installation with frequent instances of fuse box tripping with stormy wet weather and very disappointing returns for my investment compared to other 3kw systems in my area.  After many unsuccessful attempts to contact tas-solar I brought in a local electrician who found the inverter had not been set up properly - he was able rectify the problems and somehow managed to contact tas-solar who agreed to pay the costs - in writing.    I subsequently forwarded the bill to tas-solar for payment and thought no more of it until I received a final demand from the local electrical company.    All my attempts to contact tas-solar by phone, e-mail (both addresses) and facebook have failed to produce any response.  I will have to pay myself (it is not the local electricians fault) and take legal steps to recover the amount due to me.   It is a strange company indeed that doesn't answer it's phone or e-mails.",
